'' =============================================================================
'' Single-Step Debugger Test Program 12a — Multi-COG debugging (SPIN2)
''
'' Covers Test Plan test:
''   Test 12 — Per-cog debugger windows, independent stepping, COGBRK
''
'' Spin2 counterpart to the pure-PASM2 test12_multicog.spin2 — same multi-cog
'' behavior, but cog 0 runs the Spin2 interpreter (like test01), so DEBUG_MAIN
'' breaks at `main()`. The `coginit` is the FIRST statement of main(), so cog 1
'' launches within a step or two of the initial break (no long interpreter walk).
''
'' Behavior:
''   Cog 0 breaks at main() (DEBUG_MAIN) — "Debugger - Cog 0". main()'s first act
''   is COGINIT(1, @cog1code, 0), launching cog 1's PASM from hub. With
''   DEBUG_COGINIT=1 the P2 debug interrupt fires on cog 1's first instruction, so
''   cog 1 breaks on startup and a second window opens. Cog 0 then spins its own
''   counter and cog 1 spins its own, so the two windows step independently.
''
'' Expected on hardware:
''   1. Cog 0 breaks in main() — "Debugger - Cog 0" window.
''   2. Step cog 0 through the COGINIT → cog 1 launches and breaks —
''      "Debugger - Cog 1" window opens.
''   3. Stepping one window advances only that cog (x in cog 0, y in cog 1).
'' =============================================================================
CON
  _clkfreq = 200_000_000
  DEBUG_MAIN = 1
  DEBUG_COGINIT = 1

PUB main() | x
  coginit(1, @cog1code, 0)          ' launch cog 1 (PASM); DEBUG_COGINIT breaks it on its 1st instruction
  x := 0
  repeat
    x++

DAT
' ── Cog 1 : self-contained PASM image, assembled to run at cog $000 ──────────
              org     0
cog1code      add     y, #1
              jmp     #cog1code
y             long    0
